      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The heavy feeling in your jaw and neck can be quite persistent and unsettling. While it's possible that it might be related to stress or a bad tooth, it's also possible that it could be related to temporomandibular joint (TMJ) disorders, nerve issues, or even a condition like costochondritis (inflammation of the cartilage connecting the ribs to the breastbone). Consider consulting a healthcare professional, such as a dentist or an orthopedic specialist, for a proper evaluation and diagnosis.",
