    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hm okay, it's not really a sharp pain so it doesn't feel like an emergency or anything. i dont really want to go to the doctor just for some tension in my neck. if it is just stress or tmj, is there anything i can just do at home to make it go away? maybe some ibuprofen or something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While ibuprofen may help alleviate tension headaches or pain associated with TMJ, it might not address the underlying cause. For stress-related tension or TMJ, try relaxation techniques like deep breathing, meditation, or yoga to help manage stress. You can also try gentle jaw release exercises, like opening your mouth wide and releasing tension, and massaging your neck and jaw area with a foam roller or butterfleye massage.",
